  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef is the king of the kingdom named Chefland. Chefland consists of NNN cities numbered from 111 to NNN and (N−1)(N-1)(N−1) roads in such a way that there exists a path between any pair of cities. In other words, Chefland has a tree like structure.\n\nOut of the NNN cities in Chefland, KKK (1≤K≤N)(1 \\leq K \\leq N)(1≤K≤N) are considered tourist attractions.\n\nChef decided to visit exactly (K−1)(K-1)(K−1) out of KKK tourist attractions. He wishes to stay in the city iii (1≤i≤N)(1 \\leq i \\leq N)(1≤i≤N) such that the **sum of distances** of the **nearest** (K−1)(K-1)(K−1) tourist attractions from city iii is as **minimum** as possible.\n\nMore formally, if Chef stays at city iii and visits (K−1)(K-1)(K−1) tourist attractions denoted by set SSS, then, the value ∑j∈SD(i,j)\\sum_{j \\in S} D(i,j)∑j∈S​D(i,j) should be **minimum**.\n\nHere, D(i,j)D(i,j)D(i,j) denotes the distance between cities iii and jjj which is given by the number of roads between cities iii and jjj.\n\nFind the city in which Chef should stay. If there are multiple such cities, print the one with the **largest** number.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain integer TTT, the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains two integers NNN and KKK denoting the number of total cities and the number of tourist attractions in Chefland.\nThe second line of each test case contains KKK integers denoting the numbers of cities which are tourist attractions in Chefland.\nThe next N−1N-1N−1 lines contain two integers each, uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​ denoting that a road exists between cities uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​.\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case, output in a single integer the number of the city in which Chef should stay so that sum of distances to nearest (K−1)(K-1)(K−1) tourist attractions is as minimum as possible.\nIf there are multiple such cities, output the city with the maximum number.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\leq T \\leq 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤K≤N1 \\leq K \\leq N1≤K≤N",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\leq u_i, v_i \\leq N1≤ui​,vi​≤N"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
