        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Chef needs to visit 3−1=23-1=23−1=2 tourist attractions. The total distance to visit 222 tourist attractions from each of the cities is:\n\nFrom city 111: Nearest tourist attractions are cities 222 and 444 or 555. The sum of distances for these cities is 1+2=31+2 = 31+2=3.\nFrom city 222: Nearest tourist attractions are cities 222 and 444 or 555. The sum of distances for these cities is 0+3=30+3 = 30+3=3.\nFrom city 333: Nearest tourist attractions are cities 444 and 555. The sum of distances for these cities is 1+1=21+1= 21+1=2.\nFrom city 444: Nearest tourist attractions are cities 444 and 555. The sum of distances for these cities is 0+2=20+2= 20+2=2.\nFrom city 555: Nearest tourist attractions are cities 555 and 444. The sum of distances for these cities is 2+0=22+0= 22+0=2.\n\nThe cities from which the distance is minimum are 3,4,3, 4,3,4, and 555. Out of these, 555 is the highest.\nTest case 222: Chef needs to visit 2−1=12-1=12−1=1 tourist attractions. The total distance to visit 111 tourist attractions from each of the cities is:\n\nFrom city 111: Nearest tourist attraction is city 222. The sum of distances is 111.\nFrom city 222: Nearest tourist attraction is city 222. The sum of distances is 000.\nFrom city 333: Nearest tourist attraction is city 555. The sum of distances is 111.\nFrom city 444: Nearest tourist attraction is city 555. The sum of distances is 222.\nFrom city 555: Nearest tourist attraction is city 555. The sum of distances is 000.\n\nThe cities from which the distance is minimum are 222 and 555. Out of these, 555 is the highest."
